# Docker Swarm Cluster Setup Using VirtualBox + Vagrant (Step-by-Step)

## Architecture

```text
Ubuntu Laptop
│
├── manager-vm   (Docker Swarm Manager)
├── worker1-vm   (Docker Swarm Worker)
└── worker2-vm   (Docker Swarm Worker)
```

---

# Step 1: Install VirtualBox

Update Ubuntu

```bash
sudo apt update
```

Install VirtualBox

```bash
sudo apt install -y virtualbox
```

Verify

```bash
vboxmanage --version
```

Expected Output

```text
7.x.x
```

---

# Step 2: Install Vagrant

### Add HashiCorp GPG Key

```bash
curl -fsSL https://apt.releases.hashicorp.com/gpg | \
sudo gpg --dearmor -o /usr/share/keyrings/hashicorp-archive-keyring.gpg
```

### Add Repository

```bash
echo "deb [signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/hashicorp-archive-keyring.gpg] \
https://apt.releases.hashicorp.com $(lsb_release -cs) main" | \
sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/hashicorp.list
```

### Install Vagrant

```bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y vagrant
```

Verify

```bash
vagrant --version
```

Expected Output

```text
Vagrant 2.x.x
```

---

# Step 3: Create Project Folder

```bash
mkdir docker-swarm-vms
cd docker-swarm-vms
```

---

# Step 4: Create Vagrantfile

```bash
vagrant init
```

Open

```bash
nano Vagrantfile
```

Delete everything and paste:

```ruby
Vagrant.configure("2") do |config|

  config.vm.box = "ubuntu/jammy64"

  config.vm.define "manager-vm" do |manager|
    manager.vm.hostname = "manager-vm"
    manager.vm.network "private_network", ip: "192.168.56.10"

    manager.vm.provider "virtualbox" do |vb|
      vb.memory = 2048
      vb.cpus = 2
    end
  end

  config.vm.define "worker1-vm" do |worker1|
    worker1.vm.hostname = "worker1-vm"
    worker1.vm.network "private_network", ip: "192.168.56.11"

    worker1.vm.provider "virtualbox" do |vb|
      vb.memory = 1024
      vb.cpus = 1
    end
  end

  config.vm.define "worker2-vm" do |worker2|
    worker2.vm.hostname = "worker2-vm"
    worker2.vm.network "private_network", ip: "192.168.56.12"

    worker2.vm.provider "virtualbox" do |vb|
      vb.memory = 1024
      vb.cpus = 1
    end
  end

end
```

Save

```text
CTRL+O
ENTER
CTRL+X
```

---

# Step 5: Create All VMs

```bash
vagrant up
```

Check status

```bash
vagrant status
```

Expected

```text
manager-vm running
worker1-vm running
worker2-vm running
```

---

# If KVM Error Comes

```bash
sudo nano /etc/modprobe.d/blacklist-kvm.conf
```

Paste

```text
blacklist kvm
blacklist kvm_intel
blacklist kvm_amd
```

Save

```text
CTRL+O
ENTER
CTRL+X
```

Update

```bash
sudo update-initramfs -u
```

Restart

```bash
sudo reboot
```

Verify

```bash
lsmod | grep kvm
```

No output means KVM is disabled.

Run

```bash
cd ~/docker-swarm-vms
vagrant up
```

---

# Step 6: Login into Manager

```bash
vagrant ssh manager-vm
```

Open another terminal

```bash
cd ~/docker-swarm-vms
vagrant ssh worker1-vm
```

Open another terminal

```bash
cd ~/docker-swarm-vms
vagrant ssh worker2-vm
```

Now you have

```text
Terminal-1 → Manager
Terminal-2 → Worker1
Terminal-3 → Worker2
```

---

# Step 7: Install Docker (Run on ALL 3 VMs)

```bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y docker.io
sudo systemctl enable docker
sudo systemctl start docker
sudo usermod -aG docker $USER
```

Logout

```bash
logout
```

Login again

Manager

```bash
vagrant ssh manager-vm
```

Worker1

```bash
vagrant ssh worker1-vm
```

Worker2

```bash
vagrant ssh worker2-vm
```

Verify

```bash
docker --version
```

---

# Step 8: Initialize Swarm (Manager Only)

```bash
docker swarm init --advertise-addr 192.168.56.10
```

Output

```text
Swarm initialized

docker swarm join --token SWMTKN-1-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx \
192.168.56.10:2377
```

Copy the join command.

---

# Step 9: Join Worker1

Run the copied command

```bash
docker swarm join --token SWMTKN-1-xxxxxxxx \
192.168.56.10:2377
```

Output

```text
This node joined a swarm as a worker.
```

---

# Step 10: Join Worker2

Run the same command

```bash
docker swarm join --token SWMTKN-1-xxxxxxxx \
192.168.56.10:2377
```

Output

```text
This node joined a swarm as a worker.
```

---

# Step 11: Verify Cluster

Run on Manager

```bash
docker node ls
```

Output

```text
HOSTNAME       STATUS   MANAGER STATUS

manager-vm     Ready    Leader
worker1-vm     Ready
worker2-vm     Ready
```

---

# Step 12: Create Service

```bash
docker service create \
--name web \
--replicas 3 \
-p 8080:80 \
nginx
```

---

# Step 13: Verify Service

```bash
docker service ls
```

```bash
docker service ps web
```

---

# Step 14: Open Application

Browser

```text
http://192.168.56.10:8080
```

Nginx welcome page should appear.

---

# Step 15: Scale Service

```bash
docker service scale web=5
```

Verify

```bash
docker service ps web
```

---

# Step 16: Promote Worker (Fault Tolerance)

On Manager

```bash
docker node promote worker1-vm
```

Verify

```bash
docker node ls
```

Output

```text
manager-vm   Leader
worker1-vm   Reachable
worker2-vm   Ready
```

Now even if the manager stops, the swarm can continue with another manager.

---

# Step 17: Stop VMs

Stop one VM

```bash
vagrant halt manager-vm
```

Stop all VMs

```bash
vagrant halt
```

---

# Step 18: Delete Everything

```bash
vagrant destroy -f
```

